    <table cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0" border="0" width="100%">
    <tr>
        <td id="descriptionArea">
            <p>When a user wants to order items how they wish and they want to do so by clicking on the arrow icon  next to the order items drop down menu, the arrow icon is not clickable and the drop down menu doesn’t appear, which leads to the user not being able to change the order of items.</p>



<p>Steps to reproduce: </p>

<ul>
	<li>The user visits the link <a href="https://www.saucedemo.com/" title="smart-link" class="external-link" rel="nofollow noreferrer">https://www.saucedemo.com/</a></li>
	<li>The user inputs a valid username "standard_user" into the username" field</li>
	<li>The user inputs a valid username into the username" field, for example "standard_user"</li>
	<li>The user inputs a valid password into the password field, for example "secret_sauce"</li>
	<li>The user clicks on the "login" button</li>
	<li>The user clicks on the "arrow" icon next to the order items drop down menu</li>
</ul>




<p>Expected result: the drop down menu appears and the user can choose to order items alphabetically from A to Z or from Z to A; or by price: from the lowest to the highest or from the highest to the lowest.</p>



<p>Actual result: the arrow icon is not clickable, the drop down menu doesn’t appear and the user cannot choose how they want to order items </p>
            <br/>
        </td>
    </tr>
    </table>

